==Russian==
===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|Ru-буря.ogg|audio}}
===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|bur'a|lang=ru}}, akin to Bulgarian {{term|буря|lang=bg}}, Slovene {{term|burja|lang=sl}}, Serbo-Croatian {{term|бура|lang=sh}}/{{term|bura|lang=sh}}, Slovak {{term|búrka||tempest|lang=sk}} and {{term|búrať||to crush}}. Non-Slavic cognates include Old Norse {{term|byrr||fair wing|lang=non}}, Latin {{term|furo||I rage, rave}}, Sanskrit {{term|भुरति||stir, palpitate|tr=bhurati|sc=Deva}}.

===Noun===
'''буря''' (búrja) {{f}}

#{{meteorology|lang=ru}} [[storm]], [[tempest]]

